    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand Versioning.\n\nVersioning communicates compatibility changes to consumers. A clear semantic policy helps teams decide when to publish breaking, additive, or corrective changes.\n\nCore idea: keep the boundary explicit, validate inputs, and keep implementation details behind a small contract.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE TypeScript:\n```ts\ntype Change = \"breaking\" | \"feature\" | \"fix\";\n\nfunction nextMajor(version: [number, number, number]): [number, number, number] {\n  return [version[0] + 1, 0, 0];\n}\n\nfunction nextMinor(version: [number, number, number]): [number, number, number] {\n  return [version[0], version[1] + 1, 0];\n}\n\nfunction nextPatch(version: [number, number, number]): [number, number, number] {\n  return [version[0], version[1], version[2] + 1];\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN / practical TypeScript:\n```ts\nfunction bump(\n  version: string,\n  change: \"breaking\" | \"feature\" | \"fix\",\n): string {\n  const [major, minor, patch] = version.split(\".\").map(Number);\n\n  if (change === \"breaking\") return `${major + 1}.0.0`;\n  if (change === \"feature\") return `${major}.${minor + 1}.0`;\n  return `${major}.${minor}.${patch + 1}`;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Easy method:\nIdentify the owner, define the smallest interface, implement the simplest working path, and only then add tooling or optimization.\n\nStep 3 — Production reasoning:\nUse semantic versioning plus changelogs, deprecation windows, and migration guidance.\n\nComplexity:\nThe examples use direct lookups, loops, maps, sets, or simple transforms; the practical complexity is driven by the data size and real I/O involved.\n\nStep 4 — Failure/edge cases:\nHandle invalid input, unavailable dependencies, stale state, lifecycle cleanup, version mismatches, and partial failure according to the boundary being modeled.\n\nStep 5 — Senior interview takeaway:\nExplain why the boundary exists, what it owns, what it deliberately does not own, and the simplest alternative you would choose for a smaller system.",
